#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""riview — Reloading Image Viewer.

Watches a directory (or a single image file, R21) and displays the newest
image in it. When a newer image appears, or the displayed file is updated,
the view updates automatically. In directory mode, Left/Right step through
the settled images (pinning the display) and n returns to the newest (R23).
c starts the slide show — cycle mode: the settled images advance toward the
newer end every cycle time, wrapping from the newest to the oldest (R27);
--cycle starts in cycle mode at the oldest image (--cycle SECONDS sets the
initial cycle time) (R29); Up/Down adjust the cycle time (R28). In full-screen
mode the effective c/p/n/Up/Down keypresses give brief on-canvas feedback —
a 1 s pale-yellow overlay on a gray shade (R30). On the first
displayed load the window fits the image (--fit ratio/exact/off) and r
re-fits on demand (R24).

Specification & design: RIVIEW-SW-SPEC-AND-DESIGN.md (spec §§1–11,
design §§12–13), rev 1.7.

Single file, no pip dependencies: Python 3.10+ with system PyGObject
(GTK 4 + libadwaita) for GUI mode. `--print` and the desktop flags need no
display.
"""

